From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] selectors indexed by id, class and tag, an ancestor filter

Each element was tested against every selector of a style sheet, and a
selector whose rightmost compound matched walked up the tree for its
ancestors (a weak_ptr lock a step): for Wikipedia's article on Wikipedia
(14,000 elements, 190 KB of CSS) 12 s of parsing on the PinePhone.
- sort_selectors() files each selector under what its rightmost compound
  needs the element to have (an id, else a class, else a tag, else
  none); apply_stylesheet() visits only the lists of the element's, in
  the same order as before.
- It also lists the tags, classes and ids the compounds before a
  descendant or child combinator need (an ancestor's); apply_stylesheet()
  keeps those of the elements above, walking from the root, in a counting
  Bloom filter, and skips a selector needing one that is not there.
The same drawing (texts, positions, colors) for the pages compared.
